# Example entry for an existing Caddy on the deployment host. Copy it into your
# own Caddyfile and reload Caddy; the app publishes on 127.0.0.1:3000 (see
# docker-compose.yml), so Caddy can reach it directly and stays the only public
# listener. X-Forwarded-For / -Proto / -Host are added by reverse_proxy, which is
# what lets the app build correct absolute URLs on the public domain.
#
# If Caddy runs in a container instead, attach it to this project's network and
# use `reverse_proxy app:3000`.

wiki.example.com {
	encode zstd gzip
	header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3000 {
		header_up X-Real-IP {remote_host}
	}
}
#Only X-Real-IP is accepted,so if using a proxy (eg. Cloudflare Proxy),you should transfer the CF-Connecting-IP into X-Real-IP
#
#	header_up X-Real-IP {http.request.header.CF-Connecting-IP}
#
